Z||000000||terryk||01-19-2001||05:12 PM||||Anyone using Chris West's modified Flowmaster 40 muffler? If so, how is the noise during cruise?<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bruce||01-20-2001||12:44 AM||||I have one. It's a little deeper sounding than stock and makes a nice, but not annoying, rumble as you're cruising. I think it helps performance, but that's my opinion. I'm very happy with mine.<BR>bb||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||01-20-2001||02:17 AM||||If you can get the video I posted in the general forum, you'll get a good idea of what it sounds like.  My SE is Flomastered.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||01-20-2001||11:48 AM||||Thanks guys, I prefer to be able to hear myself think while cruising. Every Flowmaster I've heard was too loud. I have a Dynomax on my Ciera GT/SC. You can tell it's there, but a bit of hi-fi covers it up and there is no interior resonance.<P>Bruce, is there any point where it drones?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bruce||01-20-2001||10:32 PM||||Terry,<BR>Not sure what you mean by "drones." It does have a very consistent, powerful sound; but is not tedious. I've heard the 40 series made for the Grand Am will fit the Fiero. The Delta-Flow that I have is supposed to be mellower in sound.<BR>bb||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||01-21-2001||12:16 PM||||I meant a constant resonance in the passenger compartment. The Flowmasters I've been around always had some point where the sound was annoying during cruise especially at lower RPM's below 3500-4000. Since it's not a direct bolt in, I don't want to spend the time welding it in only to find it needs to come out. ||||reg||1
